{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76d.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Not ready to build.** Revision 4 closes both corrections from round 76c. One screen-check gap remains. The check can accept Morningstar’s full quote even when the reader can see only its first line. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:197) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:211)\n     2\t\n     3\t**1. Both 76c corrections are closed.**\n     4\t\n     5\t- **Extra forecast beside a card.** The check now reads the whole page. Text outside the expected header, cards and evidence groups fails. The stylesheet may generate no text, and the design requires a copy with an extra forecast immediately before `v8` to fail. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:147](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:147) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:200](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:200) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:226)\n     6\t- **Transparent list passing the timer.** The timer now requires every expected card to pass the same opacity-aware visibility check used for the evidence. A fully transparent list must miss the three-second deadline. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:197) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:227) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:252](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:252)\n     7\t\n     8\t**2. One serious finding remains.** The check reads a text node’s entire value once its element passes `checkVisibility` and has a nonzero box. A quote clipped to one line still meets both conditions. In the accepted `v8` package, Morningstar’s quote is 219 characters and its estimate comes late in the sentence. At phone width, the reader could lose the estimate while the full-text comparison and the page-width check both pass. The saved screenshot covers only the card’s top. This is a design finding. Slice 2 has no browser implementation to test yet. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:198](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:198) · [release_check.py:174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:174) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:215](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:215) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:247](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:247) · [CSS visibility algorithm](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#dom-element-checkvisibility)\n     9\t\n    10\t**3. One correction before build.** Require expanded quotes to wrap and remain fully readable at 390 px. Use the stored Morningstar entry as the test. The normal page must show its full quote when scrolled to it. A copy that clips the quote to one line must fail even though its text is identical. I found no separate forecast leak, outgoing request path or other build blocker in the specified design. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:70](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:70) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:211)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
