{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/release.py | sed -n '323,350p;442,491p'\"","aggregated_output":"   323\t\n   324\tdef _dump(value):\n   325\t    return json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')).encode('utf-8')\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\tdef stage(out_dir):\n   329\t    \"\"\"A private staging folder, unique to this invocation, beside the destination.\"\"\"\n   330\t    out_dir = Path(out_dir)\n   331\t    return Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent, prefix=f'.{out_dir.name}.staging-'))\n   332\t\n   333\t\n   334\tdef write_package(data, staged):\n   335\t    \"\"\"The data file and its manifest, written into the staging folder.\"\"\"\n   336\t    payload = _dump(data)\n   337\t    (Path(staged) / DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n   338\t    manifest = {'format': data['format'], 'allow_list': data['allow_list'], 'as_of': data['as_of'], 'data_sha256': hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()}\n   339\t    (Path(staged) / MANIFEST_FILE).write_bytes(_dump(manifest))\n   340\t\n   341\t\n   342\tdef _no_replace_rename():\n   343\t    libc = ctypes.CDLL(ctypes.util.find_library('c'), use_errno=True)\n   344\t    if sys.platform == 'darwin' and hasattr(libc, 'renamex_np'):\n   345\t        call = libc.renamex_np\n   346\t        call.argtypes, call.restype = [ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.c_uint], ctypes.c_int\n   347\t        return lambda source, target: call(source, target, RENAME_EXCL)\n   348\t    if sys.platform.startswith('linux') and hasattr(libc, 'renameat2'):\n   349\t        call = libc.renameat2\n   350\t        call.argtypes, call.restype = [ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.c_uint], ctypes.c_int\n   442\tdef check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None):\n   443\t    \"\"\"The package as a reader receives it: a real folder holding exactly the two regular files, each read once through one handle on\n   444\t    the folder; JSON with no repeated member name; a closed manifest that agrees with the data and the sha256 of the very bytes\n   445\t    parsed; data that passes `check_export` and, with the stores, `check_origins` at `expected_as_of` (or at the package's own day\n   446\t    passed through `resolve`). Returns (counts, the data checked, its size in bytes).\"\"\"\n   447\t    path = Path(path)\n   448\t    try:\n   449\t        folder = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)\n   450\t    except OSError as error:\n   451\t        if error.errno in (errno.ELOOP, errno.ENOTDIR):\n   452\t            raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: not a folder') from None\n   453\t        raise\n   454\t    try:\n   455\t        names = os.listdir(folder)\n   456\t        if sorted(names) != sorted(PACKAGE_FILES):\n   457\t            raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: holds {sorted(names)}, not exactly {sorted(PACKAGE_FILES)}')\n   458\t        raw, manifest_raw = _read_regular(folder, DATA_FILE, path), _read_regular(folder, MANIFEST_FILE, path)\n   459\t    finally:\n   460\t        os.close(folder)\n   461\t    manifest, data = _parse(manifest_raw, MANIFEST_FILE), _parse(raw, DATA_FILE)\n   462\t    counts = check_export(data)\n   463\t    _keys(manifest, 'manifest', 'the manifest')\n   464\t    if manifest['data_sha256'] != hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest():\n   465\t        raise ReleaseRefused('the manifest sha256 does not match the data file')\n   466\t    for name in ('format', 'allow_list', 'as_of'):\n   467\t        if manifest[name] != data[name]:\n   468\t            raise ReleaseRefused(f'the manifest {name} {manifest[name]!r} differs from the data {data[name]!r}')\n   469\t    if views_db is not None:\n   470\t        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else resolve(views_db, data['as_of'])\n   471\t        counts['fields_compared'] = check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, bound)\n   472\t    return counts, data, len(raw)\n   473\t\n   474\t\n   475\t# ---------- the report\n   476\t\n   477\tdef withheld_unresolved(views_db, data):\n   478\t    \"\"\"For the release report only: the number questions whose ladder does not resolve to bands, with the reason and whether the\n   479\t    view has a key. Withheld like every number question; this list never enters the package.\"\"\"\n   480\t    out = []\n   481\t    for question in data['questions']:\n   482\t        if question['class'] != 'number':\n   483\t            continue\n   484\t        bands, reason = service.ladder_bands(store.rungs_of(views_db, question['id']))\n   485\t        if bands is None:\n   486\t            out.append({'id': question['id'], 'reason': reason, 'has_key': key_measure(views_db, question['id'], data['as_of']) is not None})\n   487\t    return out\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md | sed -n '118,150p;172,179p'\"","aggregated_output":"   118\t- **The script exits non-zero when any check it names fails:** each store's day, classes and evidence; the budgets; each example; each\n   119\t  exact refusal; the forged value's identity; `v8`; each leak; the control; the closing. This run ended \"every acceptance item and\n   120\t  budget met\".\n   121\t\n   122\t**The decisive acceptance case** (council 74, `old-1`):\n   123\t- **Kept, each equal to the store and to its full text written into the script before the run:**\n   124\t  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\n   125\t  - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`, under `v4`, `v5`, `v8`);\n   126\t  - the analysts' \"$390 billion\" (`e3597`, under `v4`, `v5`).\n   127\t- **The system's own forecast** (`j1580` implied outcome, \"About $390 billion: …\"):\n   128\t  - substituted into `e2295`'s summary, it is refused with exactly \"question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store\";\n   129\t  - added to the manifest, it is refused with exactly \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\".\n   130\t\n   131\t**The other checks:**\n   132\t- **`old-1/v8`:** class `number`, marked \"Forecast unavailable\". Its 1,284 pieces of evidence are the same ids as `service.evidence` at\n   133\t  the bound.\n   134\t- **The known Yes/No leaks at their own days.**\n   135\t  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there, and\n   136\t    each package carries its own day (3,239 and 5,673 pieces of evidence).\n   137\t  - Both keep \"Yes\".\n   138\t  - The full explanation and reason texts are absent.\n   139\t  - So are the judgements' own phrases: \"around $1 trillion\", \"rung 4\", \"at rung\" and \"capex at rung\" occur in no field.\n   140\t- **Control:** event `old-1/v3` keeps \"Yes\" and its evidence, equal to the store.\n   141\t- **Closing,** on a copy of `old-1` with a closing switch for `v8`, \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\":\n   142\t  - `bundle.view_bundle` exposes it;\n   143\t  - the package shows `open: false`;\n   144\t  - the reason appears nowhere.\n   145\t  - The word \"Bullish\" does occur inside six `v8` fields: five source titles and the genuine `e1865` quote. That is source wording,\n   146\t    which the design keeps.\n   147\t\n   148\t## 3. The diagnostic search, every hit read\n   149\t\n   150\tThe search covered every decoded string of each package, ids, classes, the marker and the manifest included. For each question it\n   172\t  carries no forecast.\n   173\t\n   174\t## 4. Not shown, and still open\n   175\t\n   176\t- **The reader's screen** (slice 2, D756's screen check) is not built. The release page must read only this package, with no live\n   177\t  fetch and no idea submission, and needs a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen.\n   178\t- **The idea path in the release:** deferred (council 74); its acceptance is pending.\n   179\t- **The recorded disagreement on evidence summaries** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8) stands.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
