{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build from the available design.** I read `RELEASE-PAGE.md` end to end. Its status still says “revision 4, for council round 76d,” and its phone-width check still allows the reader to miss Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate. I could not verify revision 5. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3) · [release_check.py:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:175)\n\n1. **The two earlier fixes remain closed.** An extra forecast beside a card must fail the whole-page comparison. A fully transparent question list must miss the three-second deadline. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:200](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:200) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:226) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:252](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:252)\n2. **The one serious 76d finding remains open in this file.** A quote clipped to its first line still has a visible box. The check then reads the entire underlying text, and the phone-width check can pass because clipping creates no horizontal scroll. I found no separate forecast leak, outgoing request path, or build blocker in the available design. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:197) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:247](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:247)\n3. **Revision 5 is needed for sign-off.** The decisive test is the one 76d requested. At 390 px, expand `v8` and scroll to Morningstar’s quote. The full quote must be readable, and an otherwise identical copy clipped to one line must fail. [codex-r76d.md:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76d.md:10)"}}
